PART 1 — NON-NEGOTIABLE PRIVACY REQUIREMENTS

PDF (AIO) must remain a local-first document processing application.

These requirements are mandatory:

1. All PDF and document processing must happen locally on the user's Android device.
2. Do not introduce AI or ML features.
3. Do not introduce offline ML models either.
4. Do not add AI APIs, cloud APIs or external document-processing services.
5. Do not upload documents, images, extracted text or document metadata to external servers.
6. Do not introduce cloud storage, cloud synchronization or cloud document backups.
7. Do not add Firebase, Supabase, analytics, advertising trackers or tracking SDKs.
8. Do not introduce external OCR services.
9. Do not transmit private document information through logs, crash reports, feedback forms or network requests.
10. Do not make any document-processing feature dependent on internet access.

Prefer traditional Android APIs, Kotlin, deterministic algorithms, established local PDF libraries and classical image processing.

